Z||000006||Oreif||02-13-2001||12:59 PM||||There is no way that car went 220mph. Even if dropped from an airplane at 5000 terminal velocity of a falling object is 120mph. So the only way it could get to 220mph would be if it was being pulled (or inside) a jet aircraft. Maybe he was doing 220 kilometers per hour, That seems possible. <BR>If he would have quit trying to bury the speedo every time he drove it I bet the engine would have lasted more than 80,000 miles.  Sounds like he beat the car to death.<P>Side Note: 85 GT's only had the 85mph speedo.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-13-2001).]||||reg||13
